#> tool: awkrepl
#> wait: 22 Mary
#> pause: 40
#> must: 22 Mary    5.50  22
#> not: 20 Mark
#> source: maxline
# 8. Find the largest value and the line that holds it. Pement:
#   awk '$1 > max {max=$1; maxline=$0}; END{ print max, maxline}'
# Here on field 3 (hours). Pattern and action in one rule: when a bigger value
# comes by, remember it and the whole line. Unset 'max' compares as 0.
# Try: $3 < min won't work from an unset min; fix it with NR == 1 || $3 < min.
$3 > max { max = $3; maxline = $0 }
END { print max, maxline }

#DATA
Beth    4.00  0
Dan     3.75  0
Kathy   4.00  10

Mark    5.00  20
Mary    5.50  22
Susie   4.25  18
Susie   4.25  18
Beth    4.00  0

Kathy   4.00  10
Mark    5.00  20
